SQUARE", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491828028_1412005320916223_2885471269118461196_n.png?_nc_cat=101&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=uQ8aigt5LCIQ7kNvwHytIB-&_nc_oc=AdovBZ-Z9tdiwiXj3F9xXl_-55VM3ok0MS0ZSANgDJAXUXwUUeLBg4mkZ_bvo0H-KD0&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQSSO489sVTCKrzvNJpgofc6K9JcGkVFCpH4FLXtzGQwJA&oe=6B045F0A"}]}, "id": "2061830164498397", "locale": "en_US", "screenshots": [{"file_name": "3-seeing-eye.png", "id": "2342822843133894", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491828050_2342822846467227_8446167111981807008_n.png?_nc_cat=100&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=z4Ke56I0KiQQ7kNvwEi0V8Q&_nc_oc=Adqw2MdG39AP5NBhxW9_YXYldgC3dxvb0_xdl0jXCIkLe2Jmq8UflkfBB4JiDimurlc&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQRLoH3fmJljlfKTeB0FUYuqYtMCpO5T_o7u4RKofM0M8w&oe=6B0463AB"}, {"file_name": "4-breathing.png", "id": "1098117569656065", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491825462_1098117572989398_3569065438998971753_n.png?_nc_cat=103&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=WVyqcO8MiL4Q7kNvwFvtSu4&_nc_oc=AdqCoLJhEY_QHJvn66NMsv5_GeILyg4T5rLUmMmKii8MZ1YHtJUPkrQ_KVIu5_-KJGU&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQTB86ba1-dXMCcS-88P9Nr-_tv7i6NL5DjPYAC3C2yY2w&oe=6B04825A"}, {"file_name": "5-arm-muscle.png", "id": "3073099216361105", "uri": "https://scontent-iad6-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491825415_3073099219694438_717288193810178856_n.png?_nc_cat=109&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=1tpGesf40jAQ7kNvwEOrmNP&_nc_oc=Ado-Qi8A9qe7A0RKjK37Vp8FUNMNvrgKM1VFU6dcDyWGdRloxs11FjKcbk2HsEsYIxA&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad6-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQSw7AhzcPgTy7i1Uk0EtBztGcm1OKpPrp7LVLQggDpMCA&oe=6B046B40"}, {"file_name": "2-heart-close.png", "id": "1133964476169705", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491825546_1133964489503037_5171123759215771754_n.png?_nc_cat=104&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=0l_gSEnXxTgQ7kNvwEaJfXG&_nc_oc=Ado0_cdLvKqasgTHToo0JGilGP4el46gvUyjwfjq5QEwijZtSgizkJdlY7NaWSrxK8E&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQSXjmFRnMyJeTDPetryo1JXadzgEMrW_njeDUvCpEl1Ow&oe=6B045E0C"}, {"file_name": "1-heartbeat-lungs.png", "id": "1079259535160302", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491823757_1079259541826968_5952060383222830183_n.png?_nc_cat=104&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=rOvDo1NkJnMQ7kNvwEsj7QH&_nc_oc=Adq-nRmCTpf5cz6f3RW2ODDZj9i_xVJks0Y_CpoTepGY2MlYhXgPM0_9A5NlDKkzd2E&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQQv__gifLv-tsm4YxV00QXZfTeYI-l316tnDxlGJpE2uw&oe=6B0468DA"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "trailer-cover-2560x1440.png", "id": "3611590895670981", "uri": "https://scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491824322_3611590899004314_3689080381546488398_n.png?_nc_cat=101&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=T3lEqeJ6OTkQ7kNvwHmNxNq&_nc_oc=Adr8CSlSVgCQpnQfVrTzOTFw5heojyN3a2O8E77R8ALmI3faCyh1rypIAn0siHPWCFQ&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQRg2SAd6GELIJL9z54uoM9Ek_8JJN0M2DVwdp1k81yw9Q&oe=6B0484EE"}, "display_name": "Anatomy Cube", "keywords": ["anatomy", "xr", "human", "atlas", "male"], "long_description": "Anatomy Cube puts a life-size human body in your room, in mixed reality, or in a gallery, under a night sky or at dusk.\n\nThe body is a light glass skeleton. Carry a lens through it: a box, sphere, octahedron, dodecahedron or slice shows the full-detail anatomy inside, from about 3,500 named structures. Choose the tissues, drawing styles and colours.\n\nHOW IT WORKS: narrated sequences on the real anatomy - the senses, the heartbeat, breathing, the blood's round trip, reflexes, swallowing, moving the arm and what a stroke does.\n\nSENSORS: how each signal is made, from the body to the screen, then live: ECG leads, EEG rhythms, a pulse oximeter on the fingertip, a thermal camera reading breath at the nostrils, and an ultrasound probe you move over the skin that builds a 3D picture.\n\nIMPLANTS: placed on the atlas's own bones, vessels and nerves, part by part, with their history, materials and the non-metal alternatives - hip, knee and spine implants, bone healing, an artificial disc, a dental implant, pacemaker, heart pump, coronary stent, cataract lens, deep brain stimulation, a brain-computer interface and an NFC chip.\n\nLimits: the lens is small - about 7-9 cm with every tissue on at the chest or hand, 4 cm in the head, larger with fewer tissues. Signals and devices are simulated for teaching. Adult male model; the inner and middle ear are not included.\n\nEducational use only: not a medical device, not for diagnosis or treatment, not medical advice.\n", "short_description": "Walk around a life-size human body in your room and look inside it through a lens you carry: bone, muscle, vessels, nerves and organs in full detail. Narrated sequences show how the body works, how medical sensors read it - ECG, EEG, pulse oximetry, a thermal breathing camera, ultrasound - and how implants are placed and work, from hip and knee replacements to pacemakers, heart pumps and brain implants.\n"}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/privacy", "developer_terms_of_service_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/terms", "publisher_name": "Nebulytic", "support_website_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/support", "website_url": "https://nebulytic.com/apps/anatomy-cube/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "1043107547362485"}, {"id": "478089301798119"}], "external_subscription_type": "N